# Everything the image builds for itself, or must never be baked into a layer.
#
# node_modules is excluded deliberately: the `deps` stage runs `npm ci` against
# the lockfile, and a host tree copied in would shadow it with binaries built for
# the host's platform (electron, the sheets Rust sidecar).

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
out/
**/out/
dist/
**/dist/
release/
**/release/
apps/sheets/native/xlsx-engine/target/

# Credentials and local state. The BFF reads its keys from the environment at
# run time (docker-compose env_file), never from a file in the image.
#
# The `**/` forms are load-bearing, not belt-and-braces: .dockerignore patterns
# are matched against the whole path from the context root, so a bare `.env`
# excludes ./.env and nothing else. services/ai-bff/.env is a real file in this
# repo — `npm run start -w @genoffice/ai-bff` loads it via tsx
# --env-file-if-exists — and without these lines it is copied into the bff image
# with a live provider credential inside it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
electron-builder.env
**/electron-builder.env
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.task
.refs

# Not needed to build a web bundle.
e2e/
fixtures/
docs-archive/
notes/
example/
scripts/drivers/
**/*.log
.DS_Store
*.dmg
*.exe
*.zip
